Z||000000||Gokart||04-23-2000||03:40 PM||||Anyone else get the Accel coil from the Fiero Store? Got mine yesterday and I know you have to drill the pins out of the original bracket and put this coil in. Did so, but what are the two thin, angled at the end strips of metal for? No instructions came with about these "extra" pieces. If no one knows I'll just have to add them to my "extra pieces" box. These parts have saved me on other jobs many times <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||WisconsinGT||04-23-2000||04:30 PM||||Gokart, are you installing the coil on a V6? If so, I did not have to drill out anything when I installed mine. Please inform.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Gokart||04-23-2000||07:11 PM||||Yes, it's for my GT. It did have instructions to do so and it made sense cause it does not come with the bracket that holds the coil in place. Just has the metal shroud around it. You have to drill out the pins cause they are not bolts you can unassemble. I got it in and it works great, just a little disturbing that I still have these two thin metal bars left! The instructions said nothing about them! Is yours an Accel? Did you get from the Fiero Store?||||reg||2
Z||000003||Cooter||04-23-2000||07:21 PM||||My MSD coil also came with two small 90 degree pieces of aluminum. Likewise, nothing in the instructions about what to do with them.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Gokart||04-23-2000||08:11 PM||||Oh well, extra parts box it goes! WisconsinGT, I did respond to your reply on my "Air cleaner" topic but it's still only showing 1 reply!||||reg||1
Z||000005||WisconsinGT||04-23-2000||08:20 PM||||Thnaks for the reply. Ahh, I now see what you are talking about. Yeah, I too had to drill out the original rivits that hold the GM Coil. Inside the box that my Accel coil came in were several screws, bolts, metal things. I just put them aside and said good enough. I did the install similar to how I do other things. Trial and error. So the directions were never looked at. If you want them, I can look around to see if I can find them. Let me know. ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Oreif||04-23-2000||10:40 PM||||The metal strips are for the coil mounting in a 2.8L for F-bodies and GM s-10/s-15 trucks. They had a little different mount for the coil. These are not used for the Fiero.||||reg||1
Z||000007||mrfiero||04-24-2000||12:48 AM||||Be advised that the Accel coil may poop out on you.  Mine had about 5000 miles on it before it completely failed (cruising up Vail pass no less).  Luckily I still had the original one in the trunk, so I made it home OK.<P>Hopefully you have better luck than me! ||||reg||4
Z||000008||Gokart||04-24-2000||06:49 AM||||Yah! I hope I do. The reason I got it cause I thought it would probably out live the oem one! Will keep the spare in the trunk just in case.||||reg||1
